  ── WRONG HAPPY-DOM ───────────────────────────────────────────────

  The environment loaded, but it cannot survive this suite's own DOM
  reset (`document.documentElement.innerHTML = ''`): the <body>
  element is dropped, so `document.body` is null and every DOM test
  dies on "Cannot set properties of null (setting 'innerHTML')".

  This is happy-dom 15.x (or older). The project resolves 20.14.6,
  which re-creates <head></head><body></body> on that reset.

  The vitest VERSION is not the problem — both runners use 4.1.9. What
  differs is which install of it is launched, and therefore which
  happy-dom its peer symlink names:

    use    bun run test       -> node_modules/.bin/vitest -> happy-dom 20.14.6
    avoid  npx vitest run    -> npm-exec resolves a different vitest
                                install -> happy-dom 15.11.7

  No test in this suite is compatible with the broken document. Failures
  under it are a runner artefact — re-run with `bun run test`.

